  "body": "### What would you like to be added?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/kubernetes/klog/pull/322 added klog.KObjSlice as replacement for klog.KObjs. A version of klog with that is now in Kubernetes master.\r\n\r\nWe should:\r\n- [ ] Search/replace calls to KObjs in all of Kubernetes.\r\n- [ ] In places where the `if klogV := klog.V(5); klogV.Enabled() { klogV.Info(..., klog.KObjs(...) }` pattern was used, consider whether a direct `klog.V(5).Info(..., klog.KObjSlice(...))` call can be used instead. This is okay if there are no other parameters that are expensive to compute.\r\n- [ ] Update https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/devel/sig-instrumentation/migration-to-structured-logging.md.\r\n- [ ] When this is done, extend https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/logtools to complain about usage of klog.KObjs. This is optional. A better way would be to enable pre-merge linting where usage of *any* deprecated function becomes merge-blocking (see https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/109728).\r\n\r\n/sig instrumentation\r\n/wg structured-logging\r\n\r\n### Why is this needed?\r\n\r\nklog.KObjSlice takes constant time when called to prepare the parameter, in contrast to klog.KObjs which is linear with the number of entries it needs to handle.",
